<h2>02. Logic: saying exactly what you mean</h2>
<p>A program grants access when a person is an administrator or owns a docu=
ment. Does =E2=80=9Cor=E2=80=9D allow a person who satisfies both condition=
s? If access is granted, must the person be an administrator? Mathematical =
logic makes questions like these precise. It describes which combinations o=
f claims are true and which conclusions follow from assumptions.</p>
<p>Prerequisites are the distinction between an expression and an equation =
from Chapter 01. We need no special knowledge of circuits or programming. T=
he source connections are Chapter 3 and the proposition/predicate material =
in Chapter 1.</p>
<p><a id=3D"chapter-02-section-1"></a></p>
