in. In the prime-factorization proof, factors are at least two and smaller =
than the composite number, so they qualify. If one factor were one, the cla=
imed reduction would not progress. If a proof allows negative factors but o=
rders only natural inputs, the chosen smaller object may fall outside the o=
rdered domain.</p>
