<p><a id=3D"chapter-05"></a></p>
<h2>05. Sets, functions, relations, and finite size</h2>
<p>A database contains records, a program accepts inputs, and a graph conne=
cts vertices. To reason about any of these, we must distinguish an object f=
rom a collection of objects, an ordered record from an unordered set, and a=
 function from a general relationship. Source Chapter 4 supplies the main s=
cope; relation classifications from Chapter 10 are introduced here and deve=
loped further in Chapter 09.</p>
