elation on three vertices, a three-by-three Boolean table has a true entry =
precisely where the ordered pair belongs. Reflexivity asks for every diagon=
al entry true; symmetry asks that entries mirror across the diagonal. Trans=
itivity concerns combinations of entries, not merely a visible diagonal pat=
tern.</p>
