<h3>Stable matching</h3>
<p>Suppose two equally sized groups each have a strict ranking of all membe=
rs of the other group. A matching pairs each member with one partner. A blo=
cking pair consists of two people not paired together who each prefer the o=
ther to their assigned partner. A matching is stable if it has no blocking =
pair. Stability does not mean everyone receives a first choice or total sat=
isfaction is maximized.</p>
<p>Deferred acceptance proceeds as follows. An unmatched proposer applies t=
o the highest-ranked receiver not yet approached. A receiver keeps the pref=
erred of the new proposer and any current tentative partner, rejecting the =
other. Engagements remain tentative until no proposer is unmatched.</p>
