<p>The proposer-optimality theorem says each proposer receives the best par=
tner available to that proposer in any stable matching. A useful proof lemm=
a is that no rejected proposer=E2=80=93receiver pair can occur in a stable =
matching. Prove it by considering the first rejection that would violate th=
