<p><a id=3D"chapter-07"></a></p>
<h2>07. Infinity, diagonal arguments, and limits of computation</h2>
<p>Finite sets cannot be placed in one-to-one correspondence with proper su=
bsets of themselves. Infinite sets can. This is not a contradiction; it is =
a warning that a useful finite intuition depended on finiteness. Source Cha=
pter 8 develops infinite cardinality, the halting problem, and the logical =
foundations of sets. We use the function language of Chapter 05 and contrad=
iction from Chapter 03.</p>
