<p><a id=3D"chapter-08"></a></p>
<h2>08. Number theory and modular arithmetic</h2>
<p>Clocks wrap around, hash tables use remainders, and public-key arithmeti=
c depends on the structure of integers. Number theory asks which operations=
 remain valid under these constraints. Source Chapter 9 is unusually broad,=
 so this chapter joins divisibility, Euclid's algorithm, prime factorizatio=
n, modular arithmetic, and the mathematics behind toy cryptosystems. The cr=
yptographic examples explain algebra; they are not deployment instructions.=
</p>
