ath></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"b=
ase"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height:0.6944em;"></span><span class=3D=
"mord mathnormal">d</span></span></span></span>. This implication does not =
prove every way to recover plaintext is equivalent to factoring. The exampl=
es use tiny parameters and raw deterministic exponentiation to teach a theo=
rem. They make no claim about the security of a real encryption format or m=
odern implementation.</p>
<p>Finally, a polynomial-time SAT decision procedure would permit polynomia=
l-time factoring through a multiplication circuit. Encode unknown factor bi=
ts, require a nontrivial product equal to the target, and ask whether some =
assignment exists. Recover a witness by fixing one bit at a time, keeping a=
 bit value for which satisfiability remains possible. Use enough bits for b=
oth factors of a general input; a special balanced-semiprime setting permit=
s smaller fixed widths. This explains the connection between efficient cons=
traint solving and arithmetic search without claiming that factoring is kno=
wn to be NP-complete.</p>
<p><a id=3D"chapter-08-section-9"></a></p>
<h3>A complete jug trace</h3>
<p>With capacities three and five, obtain four units in the five-unit jug a=
s follows. Start empty, fill the five-unit jug, and pour into the three-uni=
t jug, leaving two in the larger. Empty the smaller, pour the two into it, =
refill the larger, then pour one unit into the smaller to fill it. Four rem=
ain in the larger. Every operation obeys the fill/empty/pour rules stated e=
arlier. This concrete trace supplements the divisibility criterion with a l=
egal construction.</p>
<p>The total quantity currently held need not remain constant because filli=
ng and emptying are allowed. The useful invariant is that amounts remain mu=
ltiples of the gcd, not conservation of water. Choosing the wrong invariant=
 from an superficially similar token-transfer example would give an incorre=
ct reachability argument. Model the actual transitions before selecting a p=
roperty to preserve.</p>
