<p><a id=3D"chapter-09"></a></p>
<h2>09. Directed graphs, orders, and scheduling</h2>
<p>A build cannot compile a program before its generated files exist. A cou=
rse cannot be taken before its prerequisites. These constraints form a dire=
cted graph, and the graph's paths determine which tasks must precede others=
. Source Chapter 10 develops the connections among graph reachability, rela=
tions, partial orders, and parallel scheduling. We use sets and relation pr=
operties from Chapter 05.</p>
