">=E2=88=92</span><span class=3D"mspace" style=3D"margin-right:0.2222em;"><=
/span></span><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height:0.6=
444em;"></span><span class=3D"mord">1</span></span></span></span> edges rea=
ches it. A breadth-first search explores vertices by increasing path length=
 and finds shortest paths in an unweighted digraph. It must remember visite=
d vertices to avoid cycling indefinitely.</p>
<p>The reachability relation <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mat=
