<p><a id=3D"chapter-10"></a></p>
<h2>10. Simple graphs and communication networks</h2>
<p>A graph can model friendship, conflicting exams, available job assignmen=
ts, or physical links in a network. The same drawing may support different =
questions: can every job be assigned, how many time slots are needed, or wh=
ere will traffic collide? Source Chapters 12 and 11 supply the scope. We st=
udy simple graph structure before switching networks so the matching and co=
loring arguments have established prerequisites.</p>
<p><a id=3D"chapter-10-section-1"></a></p>
