<p>Greedy coloring depends on order and need not be optimal. A triangle req=
uires three colors; an even cycle needs two; an odd cycle needs three. A no=
nempty graph is bipartite exactly when it has no odd cycle. One direction f=
ollows because a walk in a two-coloring alternates sides and cannot close a=
fter an odd number of edges. For the other, color each connected component =
by parity of distance from a chosen root. An edge joining equal parities wo=
uld, by comparing root paths, create an odd cycle.</p>
<p>Exam scheduling uses vertices for courses and edges for shared students.=
 Colors are time slots. This models pairwise conflicts; room capacity or te=
acher availability requires additional constraints. Graph coloring is usefu=
l because its assumptions are explicit, not because every scheduling issue =
is automatically represented by an edge.</p>
