<p><a id=3D"chapter-10-section-9"></a></p>
<h3>Bene=C5=A1 routing by coloring and induction</h3>
<p>A Bene=C5=A1 network combines two butterfly-like halves and offers alter=
native routes through upper and lower subnetworks. To route a permutation, =
pair packets that share an input-side choice, and pair packets whose output=
s share an output-side choice. These two collections of constraints form a =
graph on packets; each packet is incident to at most one edge of each kind.=
</p>
<p>Components are paths, even alternating cycles, or isolated doubled const=
raints. They can be two-colored. Send one color through the upper subnetwor=
k and the other through the lower. Each input pair splits, and each output =
pair splits, so no boundary switch is shared by two packets. Within each sm=
aller subnetwork, the induced routing is again a permutation. Induction rou=
tes it with congestion one.</p>
<p>The base case with two inputs is checked directly. The recursive step ad=
ds one input column and one output column, yielding <span class=3D"katex"><=
