<p><a id=3D"chapter-11-section-7"></a></p>
<h3>Minors and subdivisions</h3>
<p>A graph minor is obtained by deleting vertices, deleting edges, and cont=
racting edges. Contracting merges adjacent endpoints, followed by removing =
loops or duplicate edges if working with simple graphs. Planarity is preser=
ved by these operations: a contracted edge can be shrunk within its drawing=
 without creating a crossing.</p>
