<h2>14. Recurrences and generating functions</h2>
<p>A recursive algorithm's cost depends on smaller inputs. A sequence count=
 can depend on shorter sequences. A recurrence records that dependency; a g=
enerating function packages the whole sequence into one algebraic object. S=
ource Chapters 22 and 16 present these complementary tools. We introduce re=
currences first so the generating-function calculations solve a recognizabl=
e problem.</p>
