<h3>Formal series and analytic series</h3>
<p>Formal power series form a ring under coefficientwise addition and convo=
lution. A series has a multiplicative inverse exactly when its constant coe=
fficient is invertible in the coefficient system; over real coefficients, t=
his means nonzero. Solve inverse coefficients successively: the constant te=
rm determines the first coefficient, and each later product coefficient giv=
es a linear equation for the next.</p>
