<p><a id=3D"chapter-16"></a></p>
<h2>16. Random variables and expectation</h2>
<p>A probability space describes complete outcomes. Often we care only abou=
t a numerical feature: how many collisions occur, how long until success, o=
r how much work an algorithm performs. A random variable is the function ex=
tracting that number. Source Chapter 19 develops distributions, expected va=
lues, indicators, conditional expectation, and infinite-expectation surpris=
es.</p>
