<p><a id=3D"chapter-16-section-13"></a></p>
<h3>Fair individual predictions can yield an unfair shared pot</h3>
<p>Three players each contribute two units to a pot. They independently pre=
dict a fair coin result, and correct predictors split the pot; if nobody is=
 correct, all contributions are returned. Under independent fair prediction=
s, symmetry and conservation give zero expected net gain to each player. Ea=
ch individual prediction has success chance one half.</p>
<p>Now let two players coordinate opposite predictions. Exactly one of thos=
e two is correct on every toss. If you predict correctly, you share the six=
-unit pot with that player and gain one net unit. If you predict incorrectl=
y, you lose your two-unit stake. With each case having probability one half=
, your mean gain is <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><mat=
h xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretch=
y=3D"false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=3D"normal">/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo =
stretchy=3D"false">)</mo><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretch=
y=3D"false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi math=
variant=3D"normal">/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo><mo stretch=
y=3D"false">(</mo><mo>=E2=88=92</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo>=
<mo>=3D</mo><mo>=E2=88=92</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=3D"normal">/</mi><m=
n>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">(1/2)(1)+(1/2)(-2=
