d">=E2=88=92</span><span class=3D"mord">1/2</span></span></span></span>. Ev=
ery player's marginal correctness can still be one half; the dependence cha=
nged the payoff distribution.</p>
<p>This is the source's collusion lesson in a smaller algebraic form. In a =
shared-prize model, expected return depends on both your winning probabilit=
y and how many others win with you. Choosing less popular entries can affec=
t conditional sharing without changing the probability of the random draw i=
tself. That mathematical observation is not a recommendation to gamble; it =
identifies which random variables a complete payoff model must include.</p>
