<p><a id=3D"chapter-18"></a></p>
<h2>18. Random walks and stationary distributions</h2>
<p>A random walk changes state by a random local rule. The rule may be simp=
le while long-term behavior is surprising: a fair walk can eventually hit a=
 boundary with probability one but have infinite expected hitting time when=
 the other boundary is removed. Source Chapter 21 connects gambler's ruin t=
o graph walks and the mathematical idea behind PageRank. Recurrences from C=
hapter 14 and conditional probability from Chapter 15 supply the tools.</p>
