<p>All graph, probability, and ordering conventions are stated in the prefa=
ce and at their first substantive use. A symbol's domain is part of its mea=
ning; the same letter may be reused locally for a different quantity after =
its scope ends.</p>
<h1>Sources and scope of inspection</h1>
<p>The governing source is the user-provided <em>Mathematics for Computer S=
cience</em> by Eric Lehman, F. Thomson Leighton, and Albert R. Meyer, revis=
ed <strong>3 March 2017 at 11:21</strong>, with a 2016 copyright notice and=
 CC BY-SA 3.0 notice. It has <strong>987 PDF pages</strong>. Its source add=
ress is <a href=3D"https://courses.csail.mit.edu/6.042/spring17/mcs.pdf">th=
e 2017 MIT course PDF</a>; that URL was unavailable to the web reader in th=
is session, so the supplied local PDF determines the edition and section nu=
mbering.</p>
<p>The full document was machine-extracted for indexing. Front matter and c=
ontents were inspected, instructional headings were indexed, and selected e=
xposition/theorem/example pages were read, including material on network co=
nventions, planarity, number-theoretic ciphers, dependence in shared pots, =
infinite sums, record waiting, and stationary distributions. This is <stron=
g>partial manual source inspection</strong>, not a claim to have manually r=
ead every page or solved every source exercise. The PDF extraction and priv=
ate working files are excluded from the deliverable. The SHA-256 fingerprin=
t and exact access record are in <a href=3D"file:///C:/Users/amallick.ENGIN=
EERS/OneDrive%20-%20Unison%20Software,%20Inc/Documents/ChatGPT/Learning%20b=
efore%20leaving%20usinos/math-for-cs/sources.json">sources.json</a>.</p>
<p>The official <a href=3D"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-042j-mathematics-f=
or-computer-science-spring-2015/pages/readings/">MIT OCW Spring 2015 readin=
gs page</a> was checked on <strong>12 November 2026</strong> to confirm rel=
ated course/textbook provenance. Its edition and chapter numbering differ, =
so it was not used to replace the supplied 2017 contents. Statements in the=
 new textbook are original explanations of the mathematical subjects, with =
new worked examples rather than copied source passages.</p>
<p>The <a href=3D"file:///C:/Users/amallick.ENGINEERS/OneDrive%20-%20Unison=
%20Software,%20Inc/Documents/ChatGPT/Learning%20before%20leaving%20usinos/m=
ath-for-cs/coverage.md">coverage crosswalk</a> maps source section and subs=
ection headings to the new chapters, including source page locators and exp=
licit treatment notes. The instructional subject scope is complete; the pac=
kage is not a full solutions manual for every source exercise and is not a =
line-by-line reproduction of the source. Original Practice, Class, Homework=
, and Exam Problems are assigned as optional extensions by their section gr=
oups.</p>
<p>Historical numerical search limits, speculative cipher history, and hist=
orical statements about computing practice are not presented as current emp=
irical records. The new toy arithmetic examples make no recommendation abou=
t real security systems. The mathematical minor criterion for planarity is =
conventionally named Wagner's theorem; Kuratowski's subdivision criterion i=
s distinguished. The random-walk chapter distinguishes strong connectivity,=
 stationary uniqueness, and aperiodicity rather than treating them as the s=
ame property.</p>
<p>This course uses discrete mathematics from the source, with added algebr=
a preparation and one explicitly labeled additional sampling theorem (Hoeff=
ding). It does not claim to deliver full courses in calculus, linear algebr=
a, or modern statistical inference. Theorems whose longer proofs are not pr=
ovided are identified locally, including the four-color theorem, Stirling's=
 refined formula, the planarity characterizations, and foundational incompl=
eteness results.</p>
<p>No instructions embedded in the source document were treated as requests=
 to run software, change files, upload content, or contact anyone. No sourc=
e PDF or private workspace material is published or embedded in the learnin=
g package.</p>
